            <description>The High Resolution Imaging Science Experiment (HiRISE) camera offers unprecedented image quality, giving us a view of the Red Planet in a way never before seen.  It’s the most powerful camera ever to leave Earth’s orbit.  HiRISE offers three data sets, the Experiment Data Record (EDR) data set, the Reduce Data Record (RDR), and the Digital Terrain Model (DTM) data set.  DTMs are sets of digital elevation models along with the ortho images used to create them.</description>
