                  </edu.asu.jmars.layer.map2.WMSMapServer>
                </server>
                <title>HiRISE Frost Prob. Ls 000-010 (Seasonal frost)</title>
                <abstractText>This map includes an estimate of seasonal frost likelihood (expressed as a probability from 0-1 that frost is present within the spatiotemporal pixels) for regions spanning the edge of the seasonal frostcaps and into the mid-latitudes between Ls range [0-10]. It relies on daytime (~3pm) data acquired by the specified instrument and represents the average frost likelihood across Mars years 29-35. Note that CO2 and/or water frost may be present in a frost detection. Source data were obtained from the PDS. It is one of several frost likelihood maps generated based on Thermal (MCS/THEMIS), Spectral (CRISM), and Visible (HiRISE, CTX) data. Date of ASU ingest: 11/07/2024</abstractText>
                <categories>
                  <string-array>
                    <string>By Type</string>
                    <string>Surface Properties</string>
                    <string>Frost Probability</string>
                  </string-array>
                </categories>
